Falsifies `system_tests::user::unmap_tests::unmap_takes_one_page_and_the_frame_capability_survives_it`.

The defect: `AddressSpace::UNMAP` forgets the page-table half. It still finds the page (it asks
the tables rather than changing them) and still tombstones the record, so it answers `Ok(0)` and
`LIST` agrees with it, while the page stays mapped.

Expected to fail: the assertion that the page is gone from the tables after `UNMAP` returned 0.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs b/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
--- a/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall/address_space.rs
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
         let mut hold = crate::revoke::hold();
         // Both halves, neither short-circuiting the other: a page with no record is still a window,
         // and a record with no page is still one a later revoke would act on.
-        let unmapped = mmu::unmap_user_at(root, va);
+        let unmapped = mmu::translate_at(root, va).map(|(pa, _)| pa);
         let forgotten = hold.forget_mapping_at(root, va);
         if unmapped.is_none() && forgotten.is_none() {
             return Err(Error::BadPointer);
